downs to Lincoln's credit. They pass an old black man in rags and he's kneeling on the ground and he clasps his hands and he says, may the good Lord bless you and keep you safe, master president Lincoln. And Lincoln takes off his hat and he bows to this man and all the watching journalists and whatnot, the entourage are astonished by this. I mean, it's so telling. And Charles Coffin said it was a death shock to chivalry, meaning the the southern hierarchical ideals
